*> Implementation test of the glint of the inventory icons (54 section 19.3): MENU-PLAYER-SET takes the foil decision of the stack last decoded (PL-STACK-FOIL) into
*> the slot (PL-SLOT-FOIL of the player slots, PL-OFFHAND-FOIL of the off hand) and clears it with an emptied slot; MENU-STACK-PUT empties it with the stack;
*> MENU-STACK-FOIL reads it back (0 for an argument with no foil); UI-RENDER covers the opaque texels of the icon of a foil slot with glint quads (RL-GC-VERTEX) and none
*> for a slot without the foil or when the pack stack has no glint texture.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-GLINT-SLOTS.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 COPY CLCONST.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-ARG                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-COUNT               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ITEM                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-DAMAGE              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FOIL                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-E                   PIC -(5)9.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "PACK-STACK-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "ATLAS-BUILD" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "ITEMDEFS-LOAD" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 1 TO PL-STACK-FOIL
     MOVE 5 TO WS-ARG
     MOVE 3 TO WS-COUNT
     MOVE 2 TO WS-ITEM
     MOVE 0 TO WS-DAMAGE
     CALL "MENU-PLAYER-SET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ARG WS-COUNT WS-ITEM WS-DAMAGE
     CALL "MENU-STACK-FOIL" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ARG WS-FOIL
     MOVE "glint slots: a stack with the foil set into slot 5 shows it" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-FOIL TO WS-E
     MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E) TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "1" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "MENU-PLAYER-SET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ARG WS-COUNT WS-ITEM WS-DAMAGE
     CALL "MENU-STACK-FOIL" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ARG WS-FOIL
     MOVE "glint slots: emptying the slot clears the foil" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-FOIL TO WS-E
     MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E) TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 37 TO WS-ARG
     MOVE 1 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "MENU-PLAYER-SET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ARG WS-COUNT WS-ITEM WS-DAMAGE
     CALL "MENU-STACK-FOIL" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ARG WS-FOIL
     MOVE "glint slots: the off hand takes the foil" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-FOIL TO WS-E
     MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E) TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "1" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "MENU-PLAYER-SET" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ARG WS-COUNT WS-ITEM WS-DAMAGE
     CALL "MENU-STACK-FOIL" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ARG WS-FOIL
     MOVE "glint slots: emptying the off hand clears the foil" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-FOIL TO WS-E
     MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E) TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 40 TO WS-ARG
     CALL "MENU-STACK-FOIL" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ARG WS-FOIL
     MOVE "glint slots: an argument with no foil reads 0" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-FOIL TO WS-E
     MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E) TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1 TO PL-SLOT-FOIL(3)
     MOVE 2 TO WS-ARG
     MOVE 0 TO WS-COUNT
     CALL "MENU-STACK-PUT" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ARG WS-COUNT WS-ITEM WS-DAMAGE
     CALL "MENU-STACK-FOIL" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ARG WS-FOIL
     MOVE "glint slots: emptying a slot with MENU-STACK-PUT clears the foil" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-FOIL TO WS-E
     MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E) TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   Drawing: one slot widget (18 x 18 at 10, 10, slot 0, GUI scale 2) holding item 2 with the foil.
     MOVE 1 TO SM-WIDGET-COUNT
     MOVE WK-SLOT TO SM-W-KIND(1)
     MOVE 0 TO SM-W-ARG(1) SM-W-STATE(1)
     MOVE 10 TO SM-W-X(1) SM-W-Y(1)
     MOVE 18 TO SM-W-W(1) SM-W-H(1)
     MOVE 2 TO CL-GUI-SCALE
     MOVE 1 TO PL-SLOT-COUNT(1)
     MOVE 2 TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(1)
     MOVE 1 TO PL-SLOT-FOIL(1)
     MOVE 0 TO GT-ITEM-W
     CALL "UI-RENDER" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE "glint slots: with no glint texture no glint quads" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE RL-GC-COUNT TO WS-E
     MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E) TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 128 TO GT-ITEM-W
     CALL "UI-RENDER" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE "glint slots: a foil slot with the glint texture has glint quads" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "more" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE "none" TO TL-OBSERVED
     IF RL-GC-COUNT > 0
         MOVE "more" TO TL-OBSERVED
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO PL-SLOT-FOIL(1)
     CALL "UI-RENDER" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE "glint slots: a slot without the foil has none" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE RL-GC-COUNT TO WS-E
     MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E) TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM TEST-GLINT-SLOTS.
 COPY CLTEST.
